A trip to the cinema, a show or a day out should not cost you twice because you need someone with you. Most venues offer a **free or discounted ticket for a carer or companion**.

## In this guide

- [CEA cinema card](/support/leisure/cea-card/): a free ticket for someone to come with you to the cinema
- [Access cards and carer tickets](/support/leisure/access-cards-and-carer-tickets/): the Nimbus Access Card, Hynt in Wales, and free companion entry at attractions and heritage sites
- [Accessible toilets and the Radar key](/support/leisure/accessible-toilets/): Radar keys, Changing Places toilets and the Sunflower lanyard

## Quick tips

- **Always check before you book.** Most venues ask you to book carer tickets by phone or through an access booking line.
- Keep your **PIP, DLA or Attendance Allowance award letter** handy, as many places accept it as proof.
- Ask about **access performances**, such as captioned, audio described, signed or relaxed shows.
